A release that gives a lender time but leaves the borrower it lends to where it waited,
since it looks for borrowers only of threads on a queue, which a lender never is.
The borrower waits on another queue than its lender's virtual time says.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place waits on another queue than its virtual time says
Witness: fuzz lend-release-reaches-borrower

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -811,7 +811,7 @@ static void release(uint32_t c)
          * A lender waits on no queue, and its units may give time to the end of the chain of borrowers it lends to,
          * which alone of the chain may wait for a turn, every one between lending on.
          */
-        struct place *h = p != NULL ? place_borrower(p) : NULL;
+        struct place *h = p != NULL && p->queue != QUEUE_NONE ? place_borrower(p) : NULL;
         for (uint32_t d = 1; d < LEND_DEPTH && h != NULL; d++) {
             LOOP_BOUND(LEND_DEPTH);
             struct place *next = place_borrower(h);
